.TH ferry-send 1  Ferry "Ferry Manual"
.SH NAME
ferry\-send \- Send files and folders to a trusted or nearby device (`\-\-to`), or share one file by a one\-time TICKET
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBferry send\fR [\fB\-\-lang\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-to\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILES\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Send files and folders to a trusted or nearby device (`\-\-to`), or share one file by a one\-time TICKET
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<CODE>\fR
Interface language for this run (`en`, `pl`); overrides the saved setting
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-to\fR \fI<TO>\fR
Alias, nearby device name, Node ID or TICKET of the receiver (it must run `ferry daemon`, the TUI or the GUI). Repeat it to send to several devices at once
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIFILES\fR>
Files and folders to send (folders keep their structure)
